      "html": "<p>Colombia, Rio Magdalena.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/panaque_cochliodon_en/",
      "html": "<p>Wood eaters of this size (more than 40 cm) need large aquariums with very high-performance filtration units, since substantial quantities of excrement are produced.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/panaque_cochliodon_en/",
      "html": "<p>The vegetable part of the food should be high; cucumbers, potatoes, carrots and other vegetables are gladly eaten.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/panaque_cochliodon_en/",
      "html": "<p>Breeding attempts would be interesting to secure the species' existence in aquariums. However, even in former years, when they were not so rare, no confirmed breeding reports are known.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/panaque_cochliodon_en/",
      "html": "<p>December 2005: After years in which no Panaque cochliodon (Panaque suttoni, P. suttonorum) were imported, a few individuals are now reaching us again. Whether environmental problems or the civil war in parts of Colombia are responsible for their absence cannot be judged from a distance. It is good to see this species, not rare in former times, again. Their bright blue eyes on a black body are unique and are the special attraction of this species.</p>"
    }
  ],
